WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you play a judge
in this film.

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Play a judge, yeah.
-Did you speak to judges?

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:03.570 line:92%
Did you spend time in the court?

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I really --
It was absolutely fascinating.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I don't know
you have it here,

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's the family court.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, of course,
the family court,

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:12.746
because it's about the most
important thing in the world,

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:15.582
is considered rather less
than the criminal court,

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.583 line:92%
so it's a slightly poor cousin.

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:19.085
But, of course,
when you sit in the courtrooms,

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:19.619 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
you realize that

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
these people are presiding
over life and death

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:25.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
and watching terrible pain
and suffering.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:29.562
And she's presiding over a case
about a Jehovah's Witness boy

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's refused
a blood transfusion.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
But at the same time,
Stan Tucci, her husband,

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
has just thrown a hand grenade
into the marriage

00:00:35.602 --> 00:00:36.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said,
"I'm going to have an affair."

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it's all
about her balancing herself,

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.308 line:92%
and it -- it's Ian McEwan,

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:46.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it's very, very interesting
and sort of complicated

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:46.780 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and human, you know?

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:48.648
There's no black and white.
There's no goodies and baddies.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.583
It's -- It's all the gray areas
of our lives

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.720
where we get totally confused
and don't know what to do.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a fantastic part.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:54.654 --> 00:00:57.991
-I also noticed, of course, you
have to play piano in the film.

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-Is that --

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you have to play
some pretty serious piano,

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.562 line:92%
not just joking-around piano.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.631
Do you have skills as a pianist?
-Yeah. I --

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:07.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I can play the piano,
but I had to --

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had to learn this
so that I could play it live.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we -- we didn't pre-record
or anything like that.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:16.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, my family threatened
to throw me out

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I rehearsed so much
over six months.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, in the end, I used --
in the end, I went to rehearse

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:26.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a piano shop
on the Fulham Road.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.655 line:92%
And it was a big glass thing,

00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:30.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I would be playing
the piano,

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.993
and people would be outside
looking in at the piano,

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.696
wondering about
whether perhaps to purchase it.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.799
And perhaps, also wondering
whether if I came with it

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
in some way.
-Yeah.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:41.935 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I might have gone
with some of them, actually.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:44.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were...
-So, wait. This --

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:47.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
These are people
just walking down the street?

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:49.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They...
[ Applause ]

00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:53.213 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:55.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's very alluring.
-Alluring.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.684 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very alluring.
-Yes.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-'Cause usually,
on my first dates,

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would both have to find
someone to go on the date with

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
and find a pianist.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, if you can get both
at once...

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, that's it. Yes.
-Did you --

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
So people were just walking by
and saying,

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, is that Emma Thompson
in the window?"

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:10.997
-I don't know whether they were
thinking that, actually.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:11.431 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn't notice that,
particularly, but it was odd.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:15.835
-It seems like there's somewhere
between home,

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you were
kicked out for playing...

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:18.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But it seems like

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:19.439 size:78% position:39% line:92%
there's other options

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:20.874 size:88% position:44%
other than in the window
of an actual piano shop.

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:21.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:22.775 line:92%
I'll tell you why, though --

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause it was
a really posh piano.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And I had to play that piano.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:27.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I gotcha.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.649
So, it was all just -- I had to.
There was no --

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:30.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I had no other choice.
-All right.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:32.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, obviously, I take back
my earlier criticism.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, don't. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:35.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Don't even try. Yeah.

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:37.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Your husband is an actor.
-He is.

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was in "The Crown."
-Yes.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:39.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-First couple seasons
of "The Crown."

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:40.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Do you feel like,

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:43.930
for all British actors, like --
Dame Commander's one thing --

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.198
obviously,
that's a great accomplishment --

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:47.667
but that you also have to be
in shows about the royal family?

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:51.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, that's the true thing
to aim for?

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Clears throat ]

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:53.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did play the Queen once,
actually...

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:56.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You did play the Queen.
-...but not well -- not well.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.243 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
She -- It was really --
It was about that moment --

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you --
Do you remember that bloke

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.550
broke into Buckingham Palace...
- Yes.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...and sat
on the edge of her bed

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.352
and told her him her life story?
-Yes.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
-His life story -- that --
it was that.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:11.124
But, I mean, I watched it
and I thought, "I don't think --

00:03:11.124 --> 00:03:12.926 size:78% position:39%
I think other people
have done it better."

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:15.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
everyone's in "The Crown."

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:16.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ev-- Everyone.
-Yeah.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:17.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-It -- It's --

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.534
And I wasn't asked to be in it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:26.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I feel a bit twisted
about it.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:28.675 size:75% position:38%
But, you know, look,
I'll have my revenge

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:29.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
in some way.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think we're all
looking forward to that.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:32.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Absolutely.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're all looking forward
to that.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:35.415 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Now...

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.518 size:88% position:44%
a part you, obviously,
played with great skill,

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was fantastic,
is Nanny McPhee,

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:41.888 size:88% position:44%
which I've heard you say
is your favorite part.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that true that
it's your favorite part

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:45.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you've played?
-It sort of is, yeah.

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's wonderful.
-Yes.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:47.660 line:92%
-It's so -- such a unique thing,

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now you're trying
to adapt it as a musical.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-"Nanny McPhee."

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:53.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am.
-Now, that sounds to me

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:55.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
like a very arduous thing
to undertake.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:59.606
-Yeah, there was some famous
musical producer who once said,

00:03:59.606 --> 00:04:02.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
"If Hitler's alive,
I hope he's out of town

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
and working on a new musical."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because it's just hell,
'cause you just --

00:04:06.946 --> 00:04:09.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have to chuck it all out
and then start again,

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:12.719
and, I mean, I've been working
on it for two years already.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And does -- did you undertake
it knowing -- did you --

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.357
had enough people told you that,
when you started,

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:18.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
you thought, "This will be
a two-year process"?

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:19.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or was it --
-Yeah.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:20.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was that kind --
-Okay.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
-People would -- you'd say,
"I'm going to do this."

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.096 size:78% position:39% line:92%
[ Breathing quickly ]

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:24.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, all kind of...
[ Breathing quickly ]

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:28.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they'd sort of go,
"Mnh. Mnh."

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.936 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:30.470 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, I have --

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:32.472
-"We'll see you
in a couple of years," you know?

00:04:32.472 --> 00:04:33.439 line:92%
-Well, I look forward to it.

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:34.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have a lot of confidence
in you.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:35.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please don't let me down.
-No, I'll try.

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because that
Dame Commander stuff --

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:38.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
they can take that
right away from you.

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:39.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, absolutely.
-Yeah.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:40.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, 'cause my badge
could be stripped.

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] They can
just show up -- and, yeah.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.984 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Stripped of my badge.

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:46.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's such
a pleasure having you here.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for making the time.

00:04:47.387 --> 00:04:49.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, not at all.
[ Cheers and applause ]

